messages:
andrea: Hey team — hitting reports of Android SDK getting stuck in a retry loop when our Retrofit client sees 401s after refresh. Crash logs show a bunch of OkHttp 401s and repeated authenticate attempts. Any quick fixes?

devin: Can you paste the Authenticator/Interceptor? My gut: Authenticator is doing blocking refresh and multiple threads all refresh at once (thundering herd), or auth retries never give up.

andrea: minimal snippets:
```kotlin
// Interceptor adds header
class TokenInterceptor: Interceptor {
  override fun intercept(chain: Interceptor.Chain): Response {
    val t = tokenStore.current()
    return chain.proceed(chain.request().newBuilder().header("Authorization","Bearer $t").build())
  }
}

// Authenticator does blocking refresh
class TokenAuthenticator: Authenticator {
  override fun authenticate(route: Route?, response: Response): Request? {
    val newToken = tokenRefresher.refreshSync() // may retry internally
    tokenStore.save(newToken)
    return response.request.newBuilder().header("Authorization","Bearer $newToken").build()
  }
}
```

andrea: logs: 
W/OkHttp: response for call was 401
I/TokenAuthenticator: refresh start
E/Refresh: socket timeout
I/TokenAuthenticator: refresh retry
I/TokenAuthenticator: refresh done
W/OkHttp: response for call was 401
I/TokenAuthenticator: refresh start
...

sam: yep that's classic. Authenticator gets invoked for every challenge; if refresh fails transiently you'll loop. Quick options: (1) add a marker header to stop multiple authenticate attempts, (2) do single-flight refresh so only one thread refreshes and others wait, (3) make authenticate return null on failed refresh so the 401 surfaces.

devin: suggested small patch:
```kotlin
override fun authenticate(route: Route?, response: Response): Request? {
  if (response.request.header("X-Auth-Attempt") != null) return null
  val newToken = try { tokenRefresher.refreshSync(limitRetries = 2) } catch (e: Exception) { return null }
  return response.request.newBuilder().header("Authorization","Bearer $newToken").header("X-Auth-Attempt","1").build()
}
```

sam: also set retryOnConnectionFailure(false) for critical calls and ensure tokenRefresher itself doesn't block forever. For coroutine-based refresh, use a blocking single-flight wrapper (runBlocking with timeout) when calling from Authenticator.

andrea: implemented marker header + 2-retry limit + fail-fast. Pushing a canary and adding an integration test that simulates refresh endpoint flapping. Thanks!

